  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+20 & =A(x+4)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-4$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-4)+20 & =A(-4+4)+B \\\\ -8 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)+20 & =A(0+4)-8 \\\\ 20 & =4A-8 \\\\ 28 & =4A \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=7$ and $B=-8.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
